How Python code executes
-->Python code runs line by line (interpreter-based)

-->No need to compile manually--interpreter handles it.

-->Each line converted into bytecode,then executed by the Python Virtual Machine(PVM).

-->Errors stop execution immediately.

-->Example:
          print('hello')
          print('World')


***Variables & Memory Concept

-->Variable = name that stores a value in memory.

-->In Python, Variables are used to store data that can be referenced and manipulated during program execution 

-->Example:
      x = 10
      y = 'Hello'

-->Python automatically decides the datatype.

-->Vsriables are references(labels) pointing to memory objects.object

-->Use id() to check memory location:
       print(id(x))